Package: hvtiRpropensity
Type: Package
Title: Propensity Score Methods for HVTI CORR Research at the Cleveland Clinic
Version: 0.1.11
Date: 2026-10-07
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "John", "Ehrlinger",
      email = "john.ehrlinger@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
URL: https://github.com/ehrlinger/hvtiRpropensity, https://ehrlinger.github.io/hvtiRpropensity/
BugReports: https://github.com/ehrlinger/hvtiRpropensity/issues
Description: Propensity score estimation, matching, and inverse-probability
    treatment weighting (IPTW) for clinical investigations by the
    Cardiovascular Outcomes, Registries and Research (CORR) group within The
    Heart & Vascular Institute (HVTI) at the Cleveland Clinic. Provides a
    consistent two-step workflow: construct a scored or weighted dataset, then
    inspect the results or pass them downstream. Balance diagnostics
    (standardized mean difference (SMD) tables, effective sample size) are
    compatible with the plotting functions in 'hvtiPlotR'. The propensity
    score follows Rosenbaum and Rubin (1983) <doi:10.1093/biomet/70.1.41>.
